## Shared working tree — the coordination lane

**This tree is shared, and not only with you.** Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode,
WorkBuddy and GLM all edit these same files at the same time. A peer's
half-finished edit that you overwrite is work that cannot be recovered from any
transcript. The repo keeps a **Live Pair-Coding Coordination Ledger** at
`.ai-workflow/coordination/` — gitignored, same-machine files, so every seat sees
the others instantly with zero git churn.

**Before your first edit, run:**

```bash
node scripts/lane.mjs digest
```

It prints three things: **you** (your own resolved lane file), **every seat
holding a lock right now**, and the stale count. Then read
`.ai-workflow/coordination/review-queue.md` for open review requests.

**Do not enumerate lane files by name.** Seats are named per-session —
`claude.lane.md`, `workbuddy.lane.md`, `vs-claude--main-<hash>.lane.md`, … — so a
hardcoded list silently misses live seats. Measured miss, 2026-09-20: the
documented list named `claude.lane.md` + `codex.lane.md`; the seat actually
holding a lock on `backend/routes/bridge/bridgeIngestRoutes.mjs` was
`workbuddy.lane.md`, a third name the list never mentioned. An agent following the
docs verbatim would have read both named files, seen no conflict, and edited a
locked file.

**For the whole session:**

- **Read-before-edit** — re-run the digest before editing any file. If your target
  is under a seat's `🔒 EDITING NOW`, do not edit it. Pick another file, append a
  request to `review-queue.md`, or ask Sean.
- **Claim/release** — overwrite **your own** lane file (the path `digest` prints on
  its `me:` line) with status, exact files under `🔒 EDITING NOW`, and an ISO
  `Updated:` stamp when you start a slice; clear it when done. **Never write
  another seat's lane file.**
- **Commit safety** — never `git add -A` while another seat holds locks; stage
  explicit paths.
- **Staleness** — a lane stamped >30 min ago and still `in-progress` may be
  abandoned. Flag it to Sean; never silently seize the files.

**Enforcement honesty (measured 2026-09-20).** For Cursor, nothing here is a hook —
this rule fires because an agent reads it. The deterministic layer exists but is
wired per-harness: `scripts/hooks/lane-session-start.mjs` runs at session start
from `.claude/settings.json` (Claude Code) and `.codebuddy/settings.json`
(WorkBuddy). Full spec: `docs/ai-workflow/references/AI-PAIR-CODING-PROTOCOL.md`,
Rule 67 in `CLAUDE.md` / `AGENTS.md` / `CODEBUDDY.md`.
